hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1185","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, saying: Hushaym told us, Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man. Bin Salim, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays twelve voluntary rak’ahs on a day, not an obligatory one, a house will be built for him in Paradise.”"
"1186","Yahya bin Hakim told us, Mahboub bin Al-Hasan told us, Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of a man from the people of Taif, who was called: Al-Numan bin Salem, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habiba, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever prays to God every day,” then he mentioned something similar."
"1187","Yaqoub Al-Dawraqi told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, Al-Numan bin Salem told me, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, He said: Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith that Umm Habibah narrated to us? I said: Yes. He said: I did not see him say that except to be led to him. He said: You told us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays on the day Twelve voluntary prostrations, and a house will be built for him in Paradise.” Anbasa said: I have not left them since I heard them from Umm Habiba. Amr bin Aws said: I have not abandoned them since I heard them from Anbasa. Al-Numan said: I have not left them since I heard them from Amr. David said: As for us, we pray and leave. Ibn Ulayya said: This or something similar. Bakr said: Hushaym omitted from the chain of transmission Amr bin Aws, and the authentic hadith is the hadith of Ibn Ulayya, and it is in the second chapter, and what was narrated by Mahboub bin Al-Hasan Bob bin Al-Hasan 1127"
